  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building resilience through gender and conflict sensitive approaches South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is a five years project (July 2021 to May 2025) with an overall objective of building the resilience of targeted people in Juba through gender and conflict sensitive approaches to education, skills development and sustainable livelihoods in South Sudan.  Conflict affected adolescents, youth, women and men will be enabled to improve their knowledge and skill through safe, quality and gender responsive/sensitive education and skills development. Additionally, local leadership will be strengthened to ensure resilient education systems and sustainable livelihoods. The project is implemented in Central Equatorial State, Juba Town, in Greater Lake State, Rumbek East, Rumbek Centre and Wulu Counties and in Greater Pibor Administrative Area (GPAA) Pibor, Lekuangole and Verthet Counties.  Mixed project implementation modality will be applied in which Oxfam directly implements some activities while local partners will be also implementing some activities as well. Serving and Learning Together (SALT) will be the local partner working with Oxfam in Greater Pibor Administrative Area, Disabled Association for Rehabilitation and Development (DARD) another national partner working with Oxfam in Greater Lake State and National Education Coalition (NEC) is responsible partner in Juba.</narrative>
  </description>
